# PHASE 12 — BLOOD BANK MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

## Complete Implementation Master Prompt

### 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a comprehensive, secure and production-grade Blood Bank Management System for the existing multi-branch Hospital Management System.

The module must manage the complete blood lifecycle:

1. Blood donor registration.
2. Donor eligibility assessment documentation.
3. Donor history and donation records.
4. Blood collection scheduling.
5. Blood collection documentation.
6. Donation identification and traceability.
7. Laboratory screening integration.
8. Blood grouping and Rh typing.
9. Blood component preparation.
10. Component labelling.
11. Blood storage and cold-chain monitoring.
12. Blood inventory management.
13. Expiry and quarantine management.
14. Blood requests from clinical departments.
15. Blood compatibility and crossmatch workflows.
16. Blood reservation and allocation.
17. Blood issue and dispatch.
18. Blood transfusion traceability.
19. Transfusion reaction documentation.
20. Blood return and disposal management.
21. Blood wastage monitoring.
22. Blood stock reconciliation.
23. Donor communication and follow-up.
24. Blood Bank dashboards and reports.

The module must provide end-to-end traceability from donor and donation through components, laboratory testing, storage, allocation, issue and final disposition.

This is an operational Blood Bank management system, not a simple blood group registry or stock-counting application.

All donor eligibility, laboratory screening, compatibility decisions, release decisions and transfusion decisions must remain under authorized professional control.

The software must not independently determine donor eligibility, diagnose infection, declare blood compatible or authorize transfusion.

